function _anonymous(md) {return (md`### §3.1   The label set

Each banked frame carries seven labelled mark centres, and §3.3 scores the detector against them. They are the one part of the evaluation that must not come from the detector being evaluated.

They did once, and about one in seven was materially wrong. §4.7 is how they are measured now — a slower offline pass that runs on any frame in this bank. In the current set every one of the 112 labels is a direct measurement: 103 refined on the ring lattice, 9 from the line intersection alone, none predicted off the plane and none overruled by it. Re-measuring moved the median label 0.96px and the worst 8.30px.`);}

